Fillets: a contour carried on across a small notch in the rim it rounds
onto the next edge of that rim (mitcad#307).

A rim rounded on one side of a small notch whose edges are not rounded (a
plate's top edge along an arc of a cylinder, broken by a tapered hole
whose three top edges are 0.28 to 0.29 long, the notch 0.25 deep and 0.57
wide; the rounding's radius 0.5), the next arc of the same cylinder beyond
the notch not given: the bodies stored in the .f3d files round that arc
too, with one torus face over both arcs and the notch, cut by the notch's
faces. OCCT ended the contour at the notch, its end cut by the notch's
face, and the next arc stayed sharp (the result was invalid:
self-intersecting wires).

- ChFi3d_FilBuilder::AddAcrossNotches (BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::
  CarryChainsAcrossNotches, to be called after the contours are added):
  where a contour of constant radius R ends at a vertex V, the boundary of
  a face Fc of its end edge E is followed from V through edges that no
  contour holds, each lying within the fillet's contact distance on Fc of
  E's line or circle (R tan(a/2), a the angle between the faces' normals
  at V: the contact on Fc runs on inside Fc over the notch) and ending
  within 2R of V (the ball spans the notch), up to an edge of Fc on E's
  line or circle whose other face lies on the surface of E's other face.
  That edge is added as a contour of radius R (with its own tangent
  chain), placed just before the contour it is carried from, and the
  contours added are carried on in turn. (Where 0241 makes the two
  blends one face, the face is the later stripe's: so it is the given
  contour's, and BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::Generated of the given edge
  gives it.)
  ChFi3d_JoinAcrossNotches (0241) then joins the two ends over the notch.
  Lines and circles only; elementary surfaces of one kind that coincide
  (or one surface object) count as one surface.
- A notch wider than the ball (a groove 1 long and 0.0043 deep beside a
  rounding of 0.3) is not crossed: there the files' roundings end at the
  notch.

Upstream: new; without the call nothing changes.
